{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And they shall sell the live ox.</b> That is, when it caused damage outside its owner's domain. But if it caused damage within its owner's domain, he is exempt — the owner of the damaging ox can say to the owner of the damaged ox: your ox entered my domain, what did it come for?" "<b>And they shall divide its money and also the dead.</b> Since it was a tam (an ox not attested as a gorer) and it is not its way to cause damage, its owner had no need to watch it and was not negligent, and chance caused it for both of them. Therefore both are equal in the loss."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:40.267998371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}